#### 7. Sensitive Equality — `toStringFormat` (line 85)

```java
assertEquals("Catalog(items=1)", catalog.toString());
```

This assertion is welded to the exact `toString()` format. Renaming the field label or changing punctuation will break the test even though `Catalog` behavior is correct.

**Fix:** Assert the semantic property instead:

```java
@Test
void toStringContainsItemCount() {
    catalog.add("a", 1);
    assertTrue(catalog.toString().contains("1"));
}
```

Or, if `toString()` format is a contract, document that in the test name and accept the coupling intentionally.

